# Hard Boundaries

## Data Ownership

| Service | Owns (Read+Write) | Others Can Read | Others Cannot Access |
|---------|-------------------|-----------------|---------------------|
| Skill Orchestrator | skills/, invocation rules | All | Agent executor internals |
| Agent Executor | agents/, templates/ | Skill orchestrator (briefs) | Hook engine scripts |
| Hook Engine | hooks/, hooks.json | Claude Code (triggers) | Skill definitions |
| Eval Engine | evals/, benchmarks/ | All (read eval results) | Skill internals |
| Sprint Manager | .work/board.md, .work/backlog.md, agent_docs/roadmap.md | All (read sprint status) | Agent configurations |
| Doc Generator | docs/architecture/, agent_docs/features/, agent_docs/tech-design/ | All (read docs) | Sprint artifacts |

## Forbidden Shortcuts

1. Skill Orchestrator must never directly modify agent files in `.claude/agents/`
2. Agent Executor must never directly modify skill SKILL.md files
3. Hook Engine must never read agent internal state
4. Eval Engine must never modify skill content (read-only testing)
5. Sprint Manager must never modify architecture documents
6. Doc Generator must never modify sprint artifacts
7. No service may directly modify another service's owned files

## Cross-Boundary Rules

1. To request work from Agent Executor: Skill Orchestrator spawns via `Agent()` with structured brief
2. To read hook state: query `.claude/hooks.json` (public read)
3. To update sprint status: use Skill(sprint) — never edit board.md directly
4. To read eval results: read `evals/{skill}/workspace/` (public read)
5. All cross-boundary access through public file contracts, not direct modification
